<title>UK: ROWING-HENLEY ROYAL REGATTA RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ROWING-HENLEY ROYAL REGATTA RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HENLEY, England 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selected results on the</p>
<p>first day of Henley Royal Regatta on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Thames Cup (eights)</p>
<p>Nottingham and Union (Britain) beat Bedford (Britain) 2 feet,</p>
<p>seven minutes three seconds</p>
<p>Garda Siochana (Ireland) beat Upper Thames (Britain) three</p>
<p>lengths, 7:05</p>
<p>St.Catharines (Canada) beat Stanford (U.S.) 1-3/4, 6:58</p>
<p>Ruderriege Turnverein 1887 V. Essen-Kupferdreh (Germany) beat</p>
<p>Walton (Britain) 1-1/4, 7:25</p>
<p>Temple Cup (eights)</p>
<p>Durham University (Britain) beat Nephthys (Ireland) 1-3/4, 7:25</p>
<p>Reading University (Britain) beat Southampton University</p>
<p>(Britain) easily, 7:05</p>
<p>Queen's University, Belfast (Ireland) beat First and Third</p>
<p>Trinity Boat Club, Cambridge (Britain) 1/3, 7:10</p>
<p>Queen's College, Oxford (Britain) beat Hautes Etudes</p>
<p>Commerciales (France) 2-1/4, 7:25</p>
<p>Princess Elizabeth Cup (eights)</p>
<p>Eton College (Britain) beat The Oratory School (Britain) 2,</p>
<p>7:20</p>
<p>Hampton School 'A'(Britain) beat Monkton Combe School (Britain)</p>
<p>4-1/2, 7:18</p>
<p>Canford School (U.S.) beat St. Andrew's School (U.S.), Not Rowed</p>
<p>Out (NRO), 7:20</p>
<p>Oundle School (Britain) beat The King's School, Canterbury</p>
<p>(Britain) 1-1/2, 7:25</p>
<p>Wyfold Cup (coxless fours)</p>
<p>London Rowing Club (Britain) beat Worcester (Britain) 1-1/4,</p>
<p>7:20</p>
<p>Commercial (Ireland) beat Kingston 'B' (Britain) easily, 7:32</p>
<p>Sydney (Australia) beat Kingston 'A' (Britain) canvas, 7:42</p>
<p>Quintin (Britain) beat Thames (Britain) 2-1/2, 8:11</p>
<p>Diamond sculls</p>
<p>Gavin Smith (Britain) beat Richard Rogers (Britain) easily,</p>
<p>8:51</p>
<p>Oliver Griffiths (Britain) beat Robert Allen (Britain) 5, 9:00</p>
<p>Peter Haining (Britain) beat Derek Atkins (Britain) 1, 8:40</p>
<p>Britannia Cup (coxed fours)</p>
<p>Thames 'B' (Britain) beat Northwestern University (U.S.) 2-1/2,</p>
<p>8:00</p>
<p>Cambridge '99 (Britain) beat Marlow (Britain) 2-3/4, 7:51</p>
<p>University of Minnesota 'A' (U.S.) beat Royal Chester (Britain)</p>
<p>1-3/4, 7:40</p>
<p>Molesey (Britain) beat London (Britain) 1-1/4, 7:43</p>
</text>
